        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-05T10:15:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the PLATFORM_EC configs are reserved for use only in the top level Kconfig files, since they represent shim behaviour or other specific meaning.\nSo it might be best to drop the PLATFORM_EC_ part and use another name,",
      "revId": "56240898feb68486b3ae1333e71703d0ee7c5e6d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe5b6195_93421d52",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-07T06:51:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To use legacy EC file power/host_sleep.c, the build.mk requires config flag power-$(CONFIG_POWER_TRACK_HOST_SLEEP_STATE)+\u003dhost_sleep.o, so I added config flags PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ_HOST_SLEEP and PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ_S0IX, then shim/config_chip.h will enable CONFIG_POWER_TRACK_HOST_SLEEP_STATE.\n\nIf I don\u0027t use those two PLATFORM_EC_xxx flags, how to make this work? I tried to add CONFIG_POWER_TRACK_HOST_SLEEP_STATE directly to here, but it will be undefined by config_chip.h. I can use other names, still need a way to enable CONFIG_POWER_TRACK_HOST_SLEEP_STATE. I don\u0027t have a better idea. any suggestions?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "56240898feb68486b3ae1333e71703d0ee7c5e6d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64b999f3_72cf90ed",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-07T11:50:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The tricky thing here is that you are selectively including a legacy file into your build, so you may have to be careful if there are any transitive dependencies that this file has. It there are no external dependencies for this file, it might be OK, or it could be a very slippery slope trying to disentangle it from all the rest of the legacy code. YMMV.\n\nSo ignore the build.mk, since that is only used for the legacy build.\nInstead, the CMakeLists.txt file in the top level ec/zephyr directory should be where you reference the legacy files.\n\nSo perhaps in that file, you could add:\n\nzephyr_library_sources_ifdef(CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ_HOST_SLEEP\n        \"${PLATFORM_EC}/power/host_sleep.c\")\n\n\nThat should solve the file build addition.\nI don\u0027t think you should have to define CONFIG_POWER_TRACK_HOST_SLEEP_STATE, that seems only there to make sure the file gets included in the build.\n\nIt\u0027s tough to do this kind of migration. Sometimes it\u0027s better to drop the old stuff and redo it to avoid the transitive dependencies and reliance on all the old APIs, but by doing so, there may be new bugs and you have duplicate implementations. It\u0027s sometimes a hard judgement call which is best.",
      "parentUuid": "fe5b6195_93421d52",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 38
      },
